[{:db/id "q-114260/selection/c700f8d11f8efcb4d5adaca4943307ec7beb32a12cb40d1036833097d1b89caa" :answer/id #uuid "3d0d60d4-c808-524a-bd39-cfa7eb24e8a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114260/selection/24f4fbc4a7eed36d70a658a0f8157176ca16628f5b872e54061a669ca16c33c0" :answer/id #uuid "635742ee-51f9-52cc-9da0-9449b0337897" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function is concave up nowhere." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114260/selection/e58c3f5700f000b0c1af1d73c0dc3d1819c28f20b78f98df84bfa6c1574d32ee" :answer/id #uuid "a4b7b74a-d832-51e5-8564-65f071fc3ccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114260/selection/f53d38e2d127413fe9c180e146176c86d598403f477ed35ca737c68ca309a3f2" :answer/id #uuid "ffb500c6-43db-5af6-ae0a-64079df0da88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114260/selection/49dd955f7246aaaf8b0009bb70935ca10c0397c18703e7d61cbb9a56e3d7ae6f" :answer/id #uuid "5decf4a0-9685-5b59-9536-adb0c5339bc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114260/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc25a94-cdab-5a5a-9c48-14eeb1210853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114260/selection/f53d38e2d127413fe9c180e146176c86d598403f477ed35ca737c68ca309a3f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-114260/selection/c700f8d11f8efcb4d5adaca4943307ec7beb32a12cb40d1036833097d1b89caa" "q-114260/selection/24f4fbc4a7eed36d70a658a0f8157176ca16628f5b872e54061a669ca16c33c0" "q-114260/selection/e58c3f5700f000b0c1af1d73c0dc3d1819c28f20b78f98df84bfa6c1574d32ee" "q-114260/selection/f53d38e2d127413fe9c180e146176c86d598403f477ed35ca737c68ca309a3f2" "q-114260/selection/49dd955f7246aaaf8b0009bb70935ca10c0397c18703e7d61cbb9a56e3d7ae6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114260" :question/id #uuid "c643932b-c8cc-535d-94b8-66da48e8c389" :question/math-academy-id "q-114260" :question/problem "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}$ is concave up." :question/worked-solution "A function $f(x)$ is concave up on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =6x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave up, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)>0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n6x-6>0\\,⟹\\,x>1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave up on $(1,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114260/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b47fa40d-613a-5e9b-ba07-c9057dd1a96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344334/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "073f8123-cb98-5c22-8816-3e60cde51af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344334/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "b982f57b-4388-574a-b450-26ddcc0d466a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344334/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0eee1233-c6dc-5118-9310-93fe8b149f48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344334/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-344334/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-344334/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344334/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "7f347a15-e82a-53cf-8e47-6e7a629d6456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344334/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2397e37-cab1-5a5a-ad83-b194b672069f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344334/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-344334/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344334" :question/id #uuid "674e1510-2c32-55cc-bff1-6ee60c46a419" :question/math-academy-id "q-344334" :question/problem "Determine the **largest** interval on which the function $f(x)=6x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+4)$ is concave down.\n\nThe largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave down is\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the domain of the function is $x\\in (-1,\\infty ).$\n\nA function $f(x)$ is concave down on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)=6x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =6+\\frac{1}{x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+4} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave down, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}} & <0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}} & <\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x>-1$ we have $(x+1)^{2}<(x+4)^{2},$ and thus $\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}>\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}<\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}$ is always true in the given domain, and we conclude that the largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave down is $(\\,-1,\\infty \\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-344334/field-1" "q-344334/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b47fa40d-613a-5e9b-ba07-c9057dd1a96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344334"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264/selection/e58c3f5700f000b0c1af1d73c0dc3d1819c28f20b78f98df84bfa6c1574d32ee" :answer/id #uuid "ae1f8aa3-97c2-546c-ba84-b9400e634203" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264/selection/fda3e401b6a07bacc5bef7db342a6215bc6411b349a35fdc641a165d440d15ad" :answer/id #uuid "7dbc211b-d700-5c2b-a41c-d50d81c70814" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264/selection/680ec8692b6fc95fb2227343f14aa1568389f35ada9f43a9c2656345cc979f2a" :answer/id #uuid "c3fbd523-d309-565b-a178-9af0d2d74f92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264/selection/cbf73d33747e7378dc321a3a36a200c81edd3097e93e1a1f09c97cdfaea27c83" :answer/id #uuid "21cf0eeb-d81a-5899-bdd3-d7ed197c9483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264/selection/1e928af788d513570788c9949007959f4aca3fd53478e5ad2e8204a0fdc9cf13" :answer/id #uuid "338ad745-d92e-5d74-ae7b-3720d22adfc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function is concave down nowhere." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56d1b0ff-6a07-567b-9fd3-3ca303fca709" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114264/selection/1e928af788d513570788c9949007959f4aca3fd53478e5ad2e8204a0fdc9cf13" :answer-field/choices ["q-114264/selection/e58c3f5700f000b0c1af1d73c0dc3d1819c28f20b78f98df84bfa6c1574d32ee" "q-114264/selection/fda3e401b6a07bacc5bef7db342a6215bc6411b349a35fdc641a165d440d15ad" "q-114264/selection/680ec8692b6fc95fb2227343f14aa1568389f35ada9f43a9c2656345cc979f2a" "q-114264/selection/cbf73d33747e7378dc321a3a36a200c81edd3097e93e1a1f09c97cdfaea27c83" "q-114264/selection/1e928af788d513570788c9949007959f4aca3fd53478e5ad2e8204a0fdc9cf13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114264" :question/id #uuid "e55fdbac-6bb5-5bac-b529-e0d157ba40d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114264" :question/problem "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)={e}^{1-x}+2x$ is concave down." :question/worked-solution "A function $f(x)$ is concave down on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)={e}^{1-x}+2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{1-x}+2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-(-{e}^{1-x})={e}^{1-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave down, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ Notice that ${f}^{″}(x)={e}^{1-x}>0$ for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave down nowhere." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114264/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b47fa40d-613a-5e9b-ba07-c9057dd1a96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344340/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "66fa2171-1d8e-5f9a-9333-ce9602127094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344340/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9d267a85-9025-5d21-b40e-214393ef55e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344340/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e55671b9-82a2-5326-b519-bc17684c1d68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344340/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-344340/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-344340/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344340/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "463a6292-e181-5420-9f32-056cae39a71a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344340/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "03da742a-0e06-546a-92c8-9f6f0039a74b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344340/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-344340/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344340" :question/id #uuid "37de4824-560d-5bed-91bb-680586ddf82b" :question/math-academy-id "q-344340" :question/problem "Determine the **largest** interval on which the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2x+4}$ is concave up.\n\nThe largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave up is\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the domain of the function is $x\\ne -2.$\n\nA function $f(x)$ is concave up on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2x+4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{(2x)(2x+4)-2{x}^{2}}{(2x+4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(x+4)}{(2x+4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+8x}{(2x+4)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{(4x+8)(2x+4)^{2}-4(2{x}^{2}+8x)(2x+4)}{(2x+4)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(x+2)^{2}-8{x}^{2}-32x}{(2x+4)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{2}+32x+32-8{x}^{2}-32x}{(2x+4)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{3}} \\\\  & =4(x+2)^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave up, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+2)^{-3} & >0 \\\\ (x+2)^{-3} & >0 \\\\ x+2 & >0 \\\\ x & >-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave up on $(\\,-2,\\infty \\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-344340/field-1" "q-344340/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b47fa40d-613a-5e9b-ba07-c9057dd1a96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344340"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344330/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "608df557-e420-5090-bc41-1b36aa8b47a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344330/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "66041a7a-060b-5392-8ff9-f42202ea03d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344330/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer-field/choices ["q-344330/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344330/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "5e59b9ca-130b-5234-bfd9-b73e48f251ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344330/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "972def23-d3a0-5f35-bddb-299a30ef9d34" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344330/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-344330/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344330" :question/id #uuid "f7f18171-79a5-5247-b3e6-61ea19eed26d" :question/math-academy-id "q-344330" :question/problem "Determine the **largest** interval on which the function $f(x)=-3{e}^{2x}+5$ is concave down.\n\nThe largest interval where $f(x)$ is concave down is\n$(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "A function $f(x)$ is concave down on an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nFirst, let's calculate the second derivative of $f(x)=-3{e}^{2x}+5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-6{e}^{2x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-12{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find where the function is concave down, we solve the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)<0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12{e}^{2x} & <0 \\\\ {e}^{2x} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is concave down on $(\\,-\\infty ,\\infty \\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344330/field-1" "q-344330/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b47fa40d-613a-5e9b-ba07-c9057dd1a96e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31228/selection/5833a119cc7d223df5a9934bcbb2247dc1ec2c6324c24b9d2af7b7d909aa6a70" :answer/id #uuid "f194090a-34e7-5c2b-abbc-19411b397161" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,2)$ and $(2,\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31228/selection/fe706b4135b6d6893b9b837b7c5a02ea4b42ae1a1962d901216bb41259446f9f" :answer/id #uuid "c44ded78-e720-5260-b84c-0946aea05651" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\infty ,-4)$ and $(-2,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31228/selection/44bac86e90c7c3ff281f90982bd4648fec9428a0c24d92336f8bda31be15b915" :answer/id #uuid "c2006862-cceb-5aa4-9929-c791e1b36076" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31228/selection/fd2867f0b691e027cc9996216b1174817981c9e6932cb93f5e9c4d580f44d7eb" :answer/id #uuid "3aa6e347-8860-58c3-a4db-e20bd94b1518" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,-2)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31228/selection/86da8d4e7f283ec41449d8afde720a0f44c86bfb1863b067ed91be4b695f6606" :answ